{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come on in, grab a seat, both of you. What's been going on?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Um, my stomach hurts, and I'm not sleeping. I don't know, doctor, it's hard to put together.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Sorry to jump in. I'm Dana, I stay over three nights a week. She's been pretty rough.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (DOCTOR): Glad you came, Dana. Ellen, tell me about the stomach pain however it comes out.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): It's up high, kind of a burning ache. It's been, I don't know, maybe three weeks? Could be longer. I can't pin the day down.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any vomiting with it, or black stools?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): No vomiting. And no black stools.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): What about fever, or chills?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I don't feel hot.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): You mentioned sleep. How has that piece been?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Awful. I haven't slept right for like two weeks. I just lie there.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (CAREGIVER): More like a month, honestly. She's up most nights, and she texts me even when I'm not there.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know which of us is right, doctor.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): That's alright. Two weeks from you, closer to a month from Dana. We'll leave it somewhere in that span, not a hard number.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): When the stomach pain hits, what do you take?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Two of the two-hundred milligram Advil, by mouth, when it really hurts. Not every day.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Anything else, a prescription or a vitamin?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, there's a blood pressure pill, but I stopped that.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Remember the name, or the dose?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. A little peach one. I quit it a while back, on my own.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I never saw a bottle. She just said she was done with it.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay, we'll leave the name open. Do you drink alcohol?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh, socially. You know, here and there.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): When you say socially, what do most nights actually look like?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, a bottle of wine most nights, perhaps. It helps me try to sleep. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): Thank you for saying it plain. No lecture from me. A bottle most nights is just enough that I'd like to check your liver, nothing more dramatic than that.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): The neighbor's dog barks half the night too, which is annoying, but that's not really why I came.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): Dogs have their own clinic. Mind if I press on your belly?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Sure, go ahead.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Soft. Tender right under the breastbone, where you said it burns. No guarding, and the rest of the belly feels fine. Blood pressure is one thirty-six over eighty-two, heart rate seventy-four, both okay.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Is it something bad? I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'm not going to call this an ulcer from the chair. It could be the wine and the Advil irritating the stomach lining, or it could be plain acid reflux. I won't pick one until the labs are back.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'd like to start omeprazole, twenty milligrams, by mouth, once a day, before breakfast, to calm the acid down.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay. Um, for how long?",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Start it now, and we'll look again at the visit. I'm also ordering liver blood tests today, a hepatic panel, on account of the wine.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hold the Advil while your stomach's sore. If you need a pain pill, acetaminophen is gentler, just stay inside what's printed on the bottle. And if the wine can ease off even a little, no pressure from me, the stomach and the sleep might both settle some.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I can put the Advil up in the cupboard and leave the wine alone on my nights.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): I'll try. I don't know if I can do the wine thing every night, doctor.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Trying is enough for now. I'll see you back in about two weeks, when those labs are in. If the pain turns sharp, or you vomit blood, don't wait on me, go to the emergency room."
 ],
